#!/usr/bin/python3
"""maluos-desktop-session: the session's view of the MaluOS host.

A per-user service (systemd --user, D-Bus activated as com.maluos.Session)
that watches what the OS already knows and tells the session about it: the
agents on this host and their units, the inference gateway (backends,
queue, the user's own policy and spend), the vault (the user's secrets and
delegations), the user's alerts in the ledger, and the memory host this
desk runs. It talks to the gateway and the vault over their Unix sockets as
the session user, so peer-credential identity applies and no token exists
in the session. Changes become desktop notifications; the current state is
one JSON document for the shell extension (maluos-session@maluos.com) and
anything else on the session bus.

  maluos-desktop-session            run (normally from the user unit)
  maluos-desktop-session --once     print the state as JSON and exit

D-Bus: com.maluos.Session at /com/maluos/Session, interface com.maluos.Session1:
  GetState() -> s (JSON)   Refresh()   AgentAction(name, start|stop|restart)
  RequestDecide(id, approve|deny, options) -> s (JSON)      answer a vault grant request (as the owner); options is an
                                                            expiry ("7d") or JSON {"expires": "30d", "level": "use", "budget": {"usd_per_day": 10}}
  UpdateAction(open|restart|refresh|apply|apply-all|auto:...)  the updates page, restart, re-read, install now (a terminal), the switches (pkexec)
  NodeQueue() -> s (JSON)  the gateway's queue and lanes now (/node/v1/queue as this user: an operator sees every call)
  signal StateChanged(s)   property Version

Slice 3: agents carry their owner (`mine` when it is the session user); the
vault's pending grant requests for the user's secrets are in the state and
become notifications with Allow and Deny buttons; the MaluOS Desk window
(maluos-desk) shows the same state.

Slice 5: software updates. `maluctl update status --json` (python3-apt, no
privileges) is read in its own thread whenever apt's or dpkg's state changes
on disk and every 15 minutes: what is pending and from where (security,
MaluOS, Mozilla, Ubuntu), what installs on its own, whether a restart is
needed. Opening the apt cache can take seconds (minutes under emulation),
so that thread never blocks the poll loop or the bus. Updates that wait
for the user become one notification with Install (GNOME Software's
updates page); a pending restart becomes one with Restart.

Slice 7: the Upgrade Manager (maluos-desk --window updates). UpdateAction
apply | apply-all open a terminal running `pkexec maluctl update apply [--all]`;
UpdateAction auto:on | auto:off | auto:set:ORIGIN:on|off | auto:reboot:on|off[:HH:MM]
run `pkexec maluctl update auto …` in a thread (polkit action
com.maluos.admin, the shell's agent asks once per session) and
leave the outcome in updates.last_action; the switches are read back from
`maluctl update status` (its `auto` block) like everything else.

Slice 8: the Agents app (maluos-agents). On an enrolled desk the office's
agents (`maluctl office agents`, endpoints.agents) ride in the state as
office.agents, refreshed after each successful heartbeat; whenever the set
of agents (local names and owners, office ids and names) changes, the
service runs `maluos-agents --sync`, which keeps one launcher per agent in
~/.local/share/applications, the Agents folder of the grid and
~/Desktop/Agents. The MaluApps catalogue (`maluctl office apps --refresh`)
is re-read after each successful heartbeat too, so the MaluApps window
and its launchers follow the office without waiting for the window's own
timer; a summary rides in the state as office.apps.

Slice 9: a grant request is decided with its parameters (level, expiry,
budget: RequestDecide's third argument may be JSON), and its notification
gains "Choose…", which opens the Credential Manager on that request. A
request filed by the gateway's refused credential lookup carries its cause
(the model call: vault.requests[].cause) and the notification says so. A
budget alert for an agent names the agent and reaches its owner's desk
("Agent research: budget nearly used (day)"); the Desk's Alerts page lists
it under the agent.

Phase 13 G5 (the forked System Monitor's MaluOS Network and Queue tabs):
the state carries `node`, the gateway's node API view of this computer
(/node/v1/status and /node/v1/keys, read as the session user: this node's
name and id, the listener, the lanes, the nodes it is paired with, the
keys it issued), when the user is an operator of the gateway; anyone else
sees {"available": …, "operator": false}. NodeQueue() reads the queue and
the lanes live for the Queue tab, which polls it every two seconds while
it is the current page; the tab's actions (cancel, priority, pause,
resume) run `maluctl gateway node …` themselves.
"""
import http.client, json, os, pwd, re, socket, subprocess, sys, threading, time, urllib.parse

